  "database": "rschema_0303",
  "nl_text": "The rschema_0303 database is designed to manage project information, including project details, acceptance criteria, sprints, messages, stories, and tasks. The Project table stores information about each project, including its creation and update times, a unique project ID, a description, and a name. The Acceptance_Criteria_Table stores acceptance criteria for projects, with each criterion having a unique ID, a description, and a status. The Sprint table tracks the progress of each project, with each sprint having a unique ID, a name, a start and end time, a status, and a project ID that links it to the corresponding project in the Project table. The Message_Event table stores messages related to each project, including a unique message event ID, a project ID that links it to the corresponding project, a subject, a version, and creation and update times. The Story table represents individual stories within each project, with each story having a unique ID, a description, a title, a status, and project and sprint IDs that link it to the corresponding project and sprint. The Task table stores tasks associated with each story, with each task having a unique ID, a description, a status, and a title, as well as a story ID that links it to the corresponding story. The relationships between these tables are established through foreign keys, with the project ID in the Sprint, Message_Event, and Story tables referencing the project ID in the Project table, and the project ID in the Story table referencing the project ID in the Project table, and the story ID in the Task table referencing the story ID in the Story table, ensuring data consistency and integrity.",
  "gold_question": "Business Requirements Description:\nThis database is for an Agile Development Management System used to manage stories (requirements), tasks, sprints (iterations), and acceptance criteria within a project. The primary features include:\n1.Manage Stories (Requirements): Create and edit stories, including story descriptions, status, story points, and titles. Assign stories to specific projects and sprints.\n2.Manage Tasks: For each story, create and assign tasks, including task titles, descriptions, and status.\n3.Manage Sprints (Iterations): Create and manage sprints within a project. Each sprint belongs to a project and includes a name, start time, end time, and status. Assign stories to specific sprints.\n4.Manage Acceptance Criteria: For each story, create acceptance criteria, including criteria ID, description, and status. Track and manage the acceptance criteria for stories.\n5.Message Event Management: Record message events related to specific topics, including event ID, subject, message reference, version, creation time, and update time. This is used for messaging and event recording within the project.\nThrough these features, the system helps teams better manage and track project progress, ensuring each story and task is completed on time and meets the acceptance criteria.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0303.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0303\nCREATE TABLE `project` (\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`project_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `acceptance_criteria` (\n  `criteria_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `description` text NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`criteria_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sprint` (\n  `sprint_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`sprint_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `sprint_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`project_id`) REFERENCES `project` (`project_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `message_event` (\n  `message_event_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `subject` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `version` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`message_event_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `message_event_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`project_id`) REFERENCES `project` (`project_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `story` (\n  `story_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sprint_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`story_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `story_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`project_id`) REFERENCES `project` (`project_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `story_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`sprint_id`) REFERENCES `sprint` (`sprint_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `task` (\n  `task_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `story_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`task_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `task_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`story_id`) REFERENCES `story` (`story_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
